{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup"],"anchor":"Checking-a-destination","title":"Checking a destination"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport"],"anchor":"Sending-without-a-network","title":"Sending without a network"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinationtesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"DestinationTesting","modules":[{"name":"DestinationTesting"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"DestinationTesting"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance"},{"type":"text","text":" runs the checks every vendor destination must pass, through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps each request and answers from a script rather than the network:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"its requests match recorded fixtures byte for byte;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is sent only after the adopter opts in, and only while the record reveals it;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"behind a tracker’s consent and ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it sends exactly the records it is handed;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"a record over the vendor’s limit is left out and reported, and the rest of its batch is sent;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429 are retried, and other failures are dropped and reported;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no request carries a trace context in its header fields, even while a tracer is active.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make it with the vendor’s limit and a closure that calls the vendor’s factory with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s plan, transport and backoff. Run each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as a test case of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import DestinationTesting","import Foundation","import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import Testing","","@Test(arguments: ConformanceCheck.allCases)","func postHogConformance(check: ConformanceCheck) async throws {","    let host = try #require(URL(string: \"https:\/\/posthog.example.com\"))","    let conformance = DestinationConformance(limit: PostHogBatchEncoder.batchLimit) { setup in","        try HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken: \"phc_test\", host: host, plan: setup.plan, transport: setup.transport, backoff: setup.backoff)","    }","    try await conformance.expect(check)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each check records a Swift Testing issue for every rule the destination breaks. A project’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tests write their assertions out in full. This one is shared on purpose, as TrackingPlanTesting’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is, so every vendor module runs the same checks.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It imports Swift Testing, so add it to test targets only. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves it out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers the module these checks test."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationSetup":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationsetup","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" check hands the vendor’s factory: the plan of the events it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends, the transport to send them through, and a backoff short enough that a retry doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hold the test up."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DestinationSetup"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup","kind":"symbol","title":"DestinationSetup","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DestinationSetup"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/writingavendordestination":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","type":"link","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing a Vendor Destination"}]},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationConformance/expect(_:sourceLocation:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationconformance\/expect(_:sourcelocation:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records an issue for each way the destination breaks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"check"},{"type":"text","text":"’s rule."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expect"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:18DestinationTesting16ConformanceCheckO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ConformanceCheck"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance\/expect(_:sourceLocation:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"expect(_:sourceLocation:)"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck":{"abstract":[{"text":"One rule every vendor destination keeps, which ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance\/expect(_:sourceLocation:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","title":"ConformanceCheck","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConformanceCheck"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConformanceCheck"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","kind":"symbol","title":"DestinationTesting","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationConformance":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DestinationConformance"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DestinationConformance"}],"title":"DestinationConformance","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationconformance","abstract":[{"text":"The checks every vendor destination passes, run from the vendor module’s tests: its requests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match recorded fixtures byte for byte, and it keeps the library’s rules for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" values,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent, oversized records, retries and trace context.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ScriptedTransport":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScriptedTransport"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPTransport"},{"type":"text","text":" that answers each request from a script and keeps every request it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: the seam a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" check sends through instead of the network."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScriptedTransport"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/scriptedtransport","title":"ScriptedTransport"}}}